{% comment %}
  The category page for a category with nothing in it.

  Two things land here:

  - A /collections/<handle> URL for a collection that does not exist, with `from_path: true`.
    Shopify answers those with the 404 template, and a mega menu row can name a category the
    store has not created yet ('menu-static-items' keeps the lists, scripts/shopify/store-config.mjs
    declares the collections). "Page not found" is the wrong thing to say about a category of the
    shop, so 'main-404' renders this instead and it says "No products found in this category"
    under the category's own name.

    Liquid cannot name that category, because Shopify rewrites the path before the 404 template
    is rendered: `request.path` is "/404" by then and the handle the shopper asked for is gone
    from every object the template can see. The browser still has it, so the heading, the
    breadcrumb and the tab title are filled in by assets/empty-category.js from
    location.pathname, and the panel only appears on a path that has /collections/ in it - any
    other dead URL keeps the ordinary 404, which is drawn right beside this and hidden by the
    class the script puts on <html>. With the script blocked, nothing here shows and the 404
    stands, which is why the 404's own blocks are still rendered.

  - A collection that is real but holds nothing, from the collection grid sections, which pass
    `category` and `compact: true` because the banner above has already printed the title. Both
    say the same thing in the same words, so a shopper cannot tell which of the two they are on.

  Accepts:
  - from_path: {Boolean} fill the heading from the URL in the browser (the 404 case)
  - category: {Collection} the collection itself, for the real-but-empty case
  - compact: {Boolean} drop the breadcrumb, the picture and the heading (default false)
  - section_settings: {Object} a section's settings, for the copy, colours, sizes and button.
    Not called `settings`, which is Shopify's own global for the theme's settings: a snippet given
    no `settings` still sees that object, so there is no telling whether a section passed its own.
  - image: {Image} optional picture above the heading

  A category the shop is about to stock says so instead of saying it is empty. The only ones
  today are the loose diamonds - see `coming_soon` below.

  Styles: assets/empty-category.css. Buttons: assets/eden-actions.css, which owns their hover.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'empty-category.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'eden-actions.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- comment -%}
  Not deferred, and before the markup below rather than in the head: the element has to be
  upgraded as the parser reaches it, so the class that hides the 404 beside it is on <html>
  before the 404's own markup is parsed. Deferred, the 404 paints first and is then swapped,
  which reads as a fault. That is what ParserBlockingScript warns about and why it is turned off
  for this one line: the file is under a kilobyte, it is served from the shop's own CDN, and the
  only page that loads it is a 404.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if from_path -%}
  {% # theme-check-disable ParserBlockingScript %}
  <script src="{{ 'empty-category.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
  {% # theme-check-enable ParserBlockingScript %}
{%- endif -%}

{%- liquid
  assign ec = section_settings

  comment
    A real collection has its title; in the 404 case there is nothing to put here yet, so the
    heading and the breadcrumb are left empty for the script to fill in and the panel stays
    hidden if it never does.
  endcomment
  assign title = category.title
  if title == blank and from_path != true
    assign title = 'Collection'
  endif

  comment
    Coming soon. The eleven loose-diamond collections - lab-grown-diamonds and the ten
    <shape>-diamonds the Diamonds menu opens - are all in the store and all empty: not one loose
    stone has been listed yet. "No products found in this category" reads as a dead end on a
    range that is on its way, so those pages say it is coming and offer a consultant and the
    rings that already carry the stones.

    A handle whose last word is "diamonds" is one of them. "stone-lab-grown-diamond" - jewellery
    set with lab-grown stones, not a loose stone - ends in the singular and is left alone. The
    same rule is in assets/empty-category.js, which has to repeat it for the 404 case: there the
    handle is only in the URL, so Liquid cannot see it (`request.path` is "/404" by then).
  endcomment
  assign coming_soon = false
  if category.handle != blank
    assign handle_tail = category.handle | split: '-' | last
    if handle_tail == 'diamonds'
      assign coming_soon = true
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Where to send the shopper instead. The handle says which family the category belongs to, and
    that family's own collection is the nearest thing to what they asked for. Every family is
    looked up in `collections` and dropped unless it is in the store and has something in it, so
    the button can never point at a second empty page. The script picks one of these by matching
    the words against the handle in the URL; a real-but-empty collection has its own handle
    matched against the same list below.
  endcomment
  assign families = 'engagement-rings:engagement|wedding-bands:wedding,anniversary,eternity,bridal,band|earrings:earring,stud,hoop,huggie,dangle,climber|necklaces:necklace,pendant,chain,charm|bracelets:bracelet,bangle,cuff|lab-grown-diamonds:diamonds|rings:ring' | split: '|'
-%}

{%- capture family_json -%}
[
  {%- assign printed = 0 -%}
  {%- for family in families -%}
    {%- assign pair = family | split: ':' -%}
    {%- assign family_collection = collections[pair[0]] -%}
    {%- if family_collection.handle == pair[0] and family_collection.all_products_count > 0 -%}
      {%- if printed > 0 -%},{%- endif -%}
      {"handle": {{ pair[0] | json }}, "words": {{ pair[1] | split: ',' | json }}, "label": {{ family_collection.title | json }}, "url": {{ family_collection.url | json }}}
      {%- assign printed = printed | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
]
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- liquid
  assign family_json = family_json | strip

  comment
    The nearest family for a real collection, worked out here rather than in the script because
    this case never reaches the script. The handle is matched against the same word lists.
  endcomment
  assign parent_label = ''
  assign parent_url = ''
  if category.handle != blank
    for family in families
      assign pair = family | split: ':'
      if pair[0] == category.handle
        continue
      endif
      assign family_collection = collections[pair[0]]
      if family_collection.handle != pair[0] or family_collection.all_products_count == 0
        continue
      endif
      assign words = pair[1] | split: ','
      for word in words
        if category.handle contains word
          assign parent_label = family_collection.title
          assign parent_url = family_collection.url
          break
        endif
      endfor
      if parent_label != blank
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    The copy. A section that has these settings decides them, and a cleared setting there means
    the merchant wants that line gone; the collection grid passes no settings at all, so the
    wording below stands for it and the two pages still read alike.
  endcomment
  assign message = ec.empty_category_message
  assign note = ec.empty_category_note
  unless section_settings
    assign note = 'Nothing is listed here just yet. New pieces are added every week, or talk to us and we will make yours.'
  endunless
  assign message = message | default: 'No products found in this category.'
  assign parent_prefix = ec.empty_category_parent_prefix | default: 'Shop'
  assign button_label = ec.empty_category_button_label | default: 'Shop all jewellery'
  assign button_link = ec.empty_category_button_link | default: routes.all_products_collection_url
  assign button_style = ec.empty_category_button_style | default: 'solid'
  assign second_style = 'outline'
  if button_style == 'outline'
    assign second_style = 'solid'
  endif

  assign show_parent = true
  if ec.empty_category_show_parent == false
    assign show_parent = false
  endif

  assign heading_size = ec.empty_category_heading_size | default: 0
  assign heading_size_mobile = ec.empty_category_heading_size_mobile | default: 0
  assign text_size = ec.empty_category_text_size | default: 0
  assign picture = image | default: ec.empty_category_image

  comment
    The coming-soon wording, and the two things to do instead of buying a stone today. These are
    also handed to the script as data attributes below, because on the 404 the handle is only
    known in the browser. The nearest-family button has nothing to offer here - every diamond
    collection is empty, so it would be dropped anyway - and its place goes to the rings.
  endcomment
  assign soon_badge = ec.empty_category_soon_badge | default: 'Coming soon'
  assign soon_message = ec.empty_category_soon_message | default: 'Loose diamonds are coming soon.'
  assign soon_note = ec.empty_category_soon_note | default: 'We are certifying and photographing every stone before it goes on sale. Tell a consultant the shape, carat and budget you have in mind and we will send you the ones that match - or choose a setting and we will set your stone in it.'
  assign soon_button_label = ec.empty_category_soon_button_label | default: 'Talk to a consultant'
  assign soon_button_link = ec.empty_category_soon_button_link | default: '/pages/book-a-consultation'
  assign soon_link_label = ec.empty_category_soon_link_label | default: 'Shop engagement rings'
  assign soon_link_url = ec.empty_category_soon_link_url | default: '/collections/engagement-rings'

  if coming_soon
    assign message = soon_message
    assign note = soon_note
    assign button_label = soon_button_label
    assign button_link = soon_button_link
    assign show_parent = false
  endif
-%}

{%- capture ec_style -%}
  {%- if ec.empty_category_band_color != blank and ec.empty_category_band_color != 'rgba(0,0,0,0)' -%}--ec-band-bg: {{ ec.empty_category_band_color }};{%- endif -%}
  {%- if ec.empty_category_heading_color != blank and ec.empty_category_heading_color != 'rgba(0,0,0,0)' -%}--ec-heading-color: {{ ec.empty_category_heading_color }};{%- endif -%}
  {%- if ec.empty_category_text_color != blank and ec.empty_category_text_color != 'rgba(0,0,0,0)' -%}--ec-text-color: {{ ec.empty_category_text_color }};{%- endif -%}
  {%- if heading_size > 0 -%}--ec-heading-size: {{ heading_size }}px;{%- endif -%}
  {%- if heading_size_mobile > 0 -%}--ec-heading-size-mobile: {{ heading_size_mobile }}px;{%- endif -%}
  {%- if text_size > 0 -%}--ec-text-size: {{ text_size }}px;{%- endif -%}
  {%- if ec.empty_category_button_background != blank and ec.empty_category_button_background != 'rgba(0,0,0,0)' -%}--eden-action-ink: {{ ec.empty_category_button_background }};{%- endif -%}
  {%- if ec.empty_category_button_text_color != blank and ec.empty_category_button_text_color != 'rgba(0,0,0,0)' -%}--eden-action-on-ink: {{ ec.empty_category_button_text_color }};{%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<empty-category-page
  class="empty-category{% if from_path %} empty-category--path{% endif %}{% if compact %} empty-category--compact{% endif %}{% if coming_soon %} empty-category--soon{% endif %}"
  style="{{ ec_style }}"
  {% if from_path %}
    data-families="{{ family_json | escape }}"
    data-parent-prefix="{{ parent_prefix | escape }}"
    data-show-parent="{% if show_parent %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
    data-soon-badge="{{ soon_badge | escape }}"
    data-soon-message="{{ soon_message | escape }}"
    data-soon-note="{{ soon_note | escape }}"
    data-soon-button-label="{{ soon_button_label | escape }}"
    data-soon-button-link="{{ soon_button_link | escape }}"
    data-soon-link-label="{{ soon_link_label | escape }}"
    data-soon-link-url="{{ soon_link_url | escape }}"
  {% endif %}
>
  {%- unless compact -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The collection hero, rebuilt: the band, the breadcrumb at its left and the category's name
      centred under it, in the colours and the padding sections/main-collection-banner.liquid
      gives a real collection. The count below it is where the grid's own count sits, and says
      what a real empty collection's count says.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="empty-category__banner">
      <nav class="empty-category__crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">{{ 'content.breadcrumb.home' | t }}</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}">{{ 'content.breadcrumb.collections' | t }}</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span aria-current="page" data-empty-category-crumb>{{ title }}</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="empty-category__title" data-empty-category-title>{{ title }}</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="empty-category__count">{{ 'products.facets.product_count_simple' | t: count: 0 }}</div>
  {%- endunless -%}

  <div class="empty-category__body">
    {%- if picture != blank and compact != true -%}
      <img
        class="empty-category__image"
        src="{{ picture | image_url: width: 600 }}"
        alt=""
        width="{{ picture.width }}"
        height="{{ picture.height }}"
        loading="lazy"
      >
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The badge is rendered on the 404 whatever the handle turns out to be, hidden, because the
      script is the only thing there that knows which category it is; it shows it if the handle
      is a diamond one. On a real collection Liquid has already decided.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if coming_soon or from_path -%}
      <p
        class="empty-category__badge"
        data-empty-category-badge
        {% unless coming_soon %}hidden{% endunless %}
      >{{ soon_badge }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <p class="empty-category__message" data-empty-category-message>{{ message }}</p>

    {%- if note != blank -%}
      <p class="empty-category__note" data-empty-category-note>{{ note }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="empty-category__actions">
      {%- if coming_soon and soon_link_label != blank and soon_link_url != blank -%}
        <a
          class="eden-action eden-action--{{ second_style }} empty-category__parent"
          href="{{ soon_link_url }}"
        >{{ soon_link_label }}</a>
      {%- elsif show_parent -%}
        <a
          class="eden-action eden-action--{{ second_style }} empty-category__parent"
          href="{{ parent_url | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}"
          data-empty-category-parent
          {% if from_path or parent_label == blank %}hidden{% endif %}
        ><span data-empty-category-parent-label>{{ parent_prefix }} {{ parent_label }}</span></a>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if button_label != blank and button_link != blank -%}
        <a
          class="eden-action eden-action--{{ button_style }}"
          href="{{ button_link }}"
          data-empty-category-button
        >{{ button_label }}</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</empty-category-page>
